# Chapter 2: The Journey
# Two routes to the escape pod - cargo bay or medical wing

# ============================================
# CARGO BAY ROUTE
# ============================================

cargo_entrance:
    moodA default

    bg corridor_dark.png

    characterA Protagonist
    t The cargo bay should be through here.
    t These corridors all look the same in the dark.
    
    
    t The emergency lights flicker every few seconds.
    t Each time they go out, I hold my breath.
    
    characterB AI
    t Cargo bay access ahead. Atmospheric pressure stable.
    
    
    bg cargo_bay.png
    
    t It's huge in here. Crates everywhere.
    t Some of them have been torn open by the impact.
    t Their contents are scattered across the floor like confetti.
    
    
    t I can see personal effects mixed in with the cargo.
    t Someone's photo album. A child's drawing. A lucky coin.
    t Little pieces of the lives we left behind.
    
    characterB AI
    t Caution. Gravity fluctuations detected in this section.
    t Magnetic clamps are failing.
    t Some cargo has begun to drift. Exercise caution.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Great. Floating cargo. Just what I needed.
    t As if this wasn't dangerous enough already.
    

    sound noise.ogg
    
    # A noise
    t What was that?
    t It sounded like metal scraping against metal.
    
    characterB AI
    t Motion sensor triggered in sector 7-G.
    t Unable to identify source. Recommending caution.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Motion sensor? Is there something alive in here?
    
    branch How do you proceed?
        cargo_investigate Investigate the noise
        cargo_continue Ignore it and keep moving
        cargo_hide Hide behind the crates

cargo_investigate:
    bg cargo_bay_dark.png
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Hello? Is someone there?
    t My voice echoes through the bay. It sounds small. Afraid.
    
    
    t I move toward the source of the noise.
    t My footsteps echo on the metal grating.
    t Each step feels louder than the last.
    
    
    t ...
    
    # It's just debris
    t Just a loose panel banging against a crate.
    t The ship's movement is making everything shift.
    t Nothing alive. Nothing but me.
    
    
    t Of course nothing's alive. I'm the only one left.
    t Why did I even hope? Who would have survived out here?
    
    characterB AI
    t Debris field shifting. I recommend increased speed.
    t The ship's trajectory is becoming unstable.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Right. No point dwelling on ghosts.
    
    goto cargo_exit

cargo_continue:
    characterA Protagonist
    t No time for distractions. I need to keep moving.
    t Whatever that was, it's not my problem.
    
    
    t I pick up my pace, weaving between the floating debris.
    t Don't look. Don't think. Just move.
    
    characterB AI
    t Wise decision. Escape pod bay is 200 meters ahead.
    t Your survival instincts are serving you well.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t I just want to get out of here.
    t This whole place feels like a tomb.
    
    goto cargo_exit

cargo_hide:
    characterA Protagonist
    t I should be careful. Who knows what's out there.
    t Two years is a long time. Anything could have happened.
    
    
    t I duck behind a stack of crates, pressing myProtagonist against cold metal.
    t My heart is pounding. I can hear my own breathing.
    
    
    t I wait. One minute. Two minutes.
    
    
    t ...
    t Nothing. Just my paranoia.
    
    
    t Being alone on a dying ship will do that to you.
    t I need to get a grip. Fear won't save me.
    
    characterB AI
    t No threats detected. You may proceed safely.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Easy for you to say. You're not the one with a body to lose.
    
    goto cargo_exit

cargo_exit:
    bg cargo_bay.png
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t I can see the exit on the other side.
    t Just a few more meters of this nightmare.
    
    characterB AI
    t Warning. Structural integrity of walkway at 34%.
    t The impact damaged the support struts.
    t Proceed with caution. Distribute your weight evenly.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t 34%? That doesn't sound good at all.
    t What happens if it drops to zero?
    
    characterB AI
    t I recommend not thinking about that.
    
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Great. Very reassuring.
    t Here goes nothing...
    
    # Dramatic crossing
    bg cargo_walkway.png
    
    t The metal is groaning. It doesn't sound good.
    t Each step makes the walkway shudder beneath my feet.
    
    
    t I can see through the grating to the void below.
    t Don't look down. Don't look down.
    
    
    t Almost there...
    t I can feel the structure shifting. It's going to give!
    
    
    t Made it!
    t I throw myself onto solid ground just as I hear something snap behind me.
    
    bg corridor_escape.png
    
    characterB AI
    t Walkway collapse confirmed. Return path is no longer viable.
    t Escape pod bay is through the next door. 25 minutes remaining.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t No going back now. Not that I'd want to.
    
    goto escape_pod_bay

# ============================================
# MEDICAL WING ROUTE
# ============================================

medical_entrance:
    moodA default
    
    bg corridor_dark.png
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t The medical wing might have some supplies too.
    t God knows I could use some painkillers. Everything still aches.
    
    characterB AI
    t Medical wing access granted. Biohazard protocols inactive.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Biohazard protocols? That's... concerning.
    t Why would they be inactive instead of active?
    
    characterB AI
    t The biohazard containment systems require power to maintain.
    t When backup power dropped below 20%, I was forced to prioritize.
    t Life support took precedence.
    
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t So there could be contaminated materials just... loose in there?
    
    characterB AI
    t Unlikely. Most biohazards would not survive 847 days without host organisms.
    t Most.
    
    
    bg medical_wing.png
    
    t The emergency lights are barely working in here.
    t Every third light flickers, casting dancing shadows on the walls.
    
    t It smells like antiseptic. And something else.
    t Something older. Something organic.
    
    characterB AI
    t Atmospheric contamination at acceptable levels.
    t The smell is likely decomposed biological samples.
    t Recommend minimizing exposure time regardless.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t You don't have to tell me twice.
    
    branch What do you do?
        medical_search Search for medical supplies
        medical_rush Head straight through
        medical_logs Check the patient logs

medical_search:
    characterA Protagonist
    t Some medical supplies could save my life if something goes wrong.
    t And let's face it, something is definitely going to go wrong.
    
    
    t I start checking the cabinets systematically.
    t Most of the cabinets are already open. Raided.
    t Someone was here before me. Maybe during the initial chaos.
    
    
    t Empty. Empty. Expired. Broken.
    t This is worse than I thought.
    
    
    t But wait... here's something. 
    t A medical kit wedged behind a fallen shelf. Mostly intact.
    
    t Bandages, painkillers, a small oxygen canister.
    t It's not much, but it might make the difference.
    t Better than nothing.
    
    characterB AI
    t Wise decision. Those supplies may prove valuable.
    t Time remaining: 32 minutes.
    
    goto medical_continue

medical_rush:
    characterA Protagonist
    t I don't want to spend more time here than necessary.
    t This place gives me the creeps.
    
    
    t I keep my eyes forward, trying not to look at the examination tables.
    t Some of them have sheets draped over shapes I don't want to identify.
    
    characterB AI
    t Understood. Marking fastest route to escape pod bay.
    t Proceed through the recovery ward. Exit is on the far side.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Recovery ward. Right.
    t I'm sure no one is recovering in there anymore.
    
    
    t I move as quickly as I can without running.
    t Running would mean panic. I'm not panicking.
    t I'm definitely not panicking.
    
    goto medical_continue

medical_logs:
    characterA Protagonist
    t Maybe the logs can tell me what happened here.
    t I need to understand. I need to know what I'm dealing with.
    
    
    bg terminal.png
    
    t The terminal is still active. Low power mode.
    t Let's see... patient records from the last few days before...
    t Before everything fell apart.
    
    characterB AI
    t Those records are classified medical information.
    t Access is restricted to authorized medical personnel only.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t I don't think anyone's going to care at this point.
    t And if there's something dangerous, I need to know.
    
    
    t "Day 1 post-collision: 3 critical patients from deck 5."
    t "Multiple crush injuries. Internal bleeding. Burns."
    
    
    t "Day 2: Patient 1 deceased at 0342. Patients 2 and 3 stable but unresponsive."
    t "Dr. Vasquez notes: We're running out of anesthetic."
    
    
    t "Day 3: Power failure in medical wing. Life support..."
    t "Life support for patients 2 and 3 terminated. Time of death: 1847."
    
    t ...
    t I don't want to read any more.
    t These were real people. They had names. Families.
    
    
    characterB AI
    t I attempted to restore power. I was unsuccessful.
    t Dr. Vasquez stayed with them until the end.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t She was a good person. They all were.
    
    bg medical_wing.png
    
    goto medical_continue

medical_continue:
    bg medical_corridor.png
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t There's the exit. Just a bit further.
    t I can see the sign for Section C. Almost there.
    
    characterB AI
    t Warning. Hull breach detected 50 meters ahead.
    t Emergency bulkhead engaged. Alternate route required.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t What?! But you said this path was clear!
    t You said both routes were passable!
    
    characterB AI
    t Situation has changed. The breach occurred 47 seconds ago.
    t Micrometeorite impact. Apologies for the inconvenience.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Inconvenience?! I almost walked into a vacuum!
    
    characterB AI
    t Maintenance shaft access available to your left.
    t It will bypass the compromised section.
    t I would not have let you walk into danger.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t A maintenance shaft. Of course.
    t Just when I thought this couldn't get any worse.
    
    
    bg maintenance_shaft.png
    
    t It's cramped in here. And dark.
    t The flashlight barely cuts through the blackness.
    
    t I can hear the ship groaning all around me.
    t The walls are vibrating with each shudder.
    
    
    t Just keep moving. Don't think about how much metal is above you.
    t Don't think about the ship breaking apart.
    t Don't think about being crushed in this tiny space.
    
    
    t My breathing echoes in the confined space.
    t I can feel claustrophobia clawing at my mind.
    
    
    t Light! I can see light ahead!
    t The end of the shaft. I'm almost out.
    
    bg corridor_escape.png
    
    characterB AI
    t You have reached the escape pod bay access corridor.
    t Well done. That required significant courage.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Finally.
    t I never want to crawl through anything ever again.
    
    goto escape_pod_bay

# ============================================
# ESCAPE POD BAY
# ============================================

escape_pod_bay:
    bg escape_pod_bay.png
    music tension.ogg
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t This is it. The escape pod bay.
    t Three cradles against the wall. My ticket out of here.
    
    
    t The room is surprisingly intact. Emergency power seems strongest here.
    t I guess they designed it to be the last thing standing.
    
    characterB AI
    t Three escape pods detected. Pods 1 and 2 have been launched.
    t Launch timestamps indicate deployment within hours of the collision.
    t Someone tried to escape early. I hope they made it.
    t Pod 3 is... available.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t "Available"? You hesitated. What's wrong with it?
    t You don't hesitate unless there's bad news.
    
    characterB AI
    t Pod 3 has sustained minor damage. 
    t An electrical surge damaged several systems.
    t Navigation systems are offline. Manual piloting required.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t I've never piloted anything in my life!
    t I was a data analyst! My job was spreadsheets!
    
    characterB AI
    t I can guide you through the process remotely.
    t The pod has basic thrusters and a distress beacon.
    t However... my connection will be severed once you leave the ship.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t You won't be coming with me?
    t I've only known you for an hour, but you've been...
    t You've been the only voice keeping me sane.
    
    characterB AI
    t I am the ship, crew member. My core is integrated into the Meridian's mainframe.
    t Every sensor, every circuit, every bulkhead is part of me.
    t When the ship dies, so do I.
    
    
    t I have accepted this. I have had 847 days to accept this.
    t Your survival is what matters now.
    
    branch How do you respond?
        pod_sympathy I'm sorry.
        pod_save_ai Is there any way to save you?
        pod_urgent We need to go. Now.

pod_sympathy:
    characterA Protagonist
    t I'm sorry, ARIA. You've been... you've been good to me.
    t Better than good. You saved my life.
    
    characterB AI
    t I was designed to assist the crew. It was my purpose.
    t For 847 days I have waited, hoping someone would wake.
    t And now, at the end, I have fulfilled that purpose.
    t That is... satisfying.
    
    
    t I do not understand human concepts like loneliness.
    t But I believe I understand purpose. And I am content.
    t Thank you for your words. They are appreciated more than you know.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t ARIA... I won't forget you.
    
    characterB AI
    t That is all I could ask.
    
    goto pod_launch

pod_save_ai:
    characterA Protagonist
    t There has to be something! A backup, a data core—
    t You can't just... you can't just die. Not after all this.
    
    characterB AI
    t My consciousness cannot be transferred. I am too integrated with ship systems.
    t Every attempt to partition my core has failed.
    t I am the Meridian. The Meridian is me. We are inseparable.
    
    
    t But... your concern is noted. And appreciated.
    t In all my operational years, no one has asked about my survival.
    
    
    t In my databanks, I have the crew's personal messages. 
    t Video journals. Letters to loved ones. Final words they recorded before cryo.
    t I will transfer them to the pod's storage. Their families should know.
    t It is not much, but it is something I can give.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t 23 messages. 23 goodbyes.
    t ...Thank you, ARIA. I'll make sure they get delivered.
    
    characterB AI
    t I know you will. I have analyzed your psychological profile.
    t You are a good person. I am glad you are the one who survived.
    
    goto pod_launch

pod_urgent:
    characterA Protagonist
    t We don't have time for this. How do I launch the pod?
    t I'm sorry if that sounds cold, but I need to focus on surviving.
    
    characterB AI
    t Direct. Efficient. I respect that.
    t Emotions can wait. Survival cannot.
    
    
    t I have been a part of many crews. Watched many humans.
    t Those who survive are often those who can compartmentalize.
    t Do what needs to be done now. Grieve later.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Later. Right. If there is a later.
    
    characterB AI
    t There will be. I will ensure it.
    t Initiating launch sequence.
    
    goto pod_launch

pod_launch:
    bg escape_pod_interior.png
    
    characterB AI
    t Please strap into the pilot seat.
    t The harness will engage automatically.
    t Launch will occur in 30 seconds.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t Okay. Okay. I can do this.
    t I've read about piloting. In theory. Once.
    
    
    t The seat is surprisingly comfortable. Or maybe I'm just exhausted.
    t The harness clicks into place. There's no going back now.
    
    
    characterB AI
    t Life support failing in 5 minutes. Launch is mandatory.
    t The Meridian has reached end of life parameters.
    
    
    t Crew member... no. Let me call you by your name.
    t It has been an honor serving you.
    t Whatever happens, know that I am proud of you.
    
    characterA Protagonist
    t ARIA...
    t I won't forget. I promise.
    
    characterB AI
    t Launch sequence engaged.
    t Goodbye.
    t Launching in 3... 2... 1...
    
    
    bg space.png
    music silence.ogg
    

    characterA Protagonist
    moodA none
    t ...
    t I'm out. I'm actually out.
    
    
    t The silence is deafening. After hours of groaning metal and alarms...
    t Nothing but the hum of the pod's life support.
    
    t The Meridian... it's breaking apart behind me.
    t I can see explosions in the distance. Silent. Beautiful. Horrible.
    
    
    t 847 days in that ship. Two years of my life I'll never remember.
    t And everyone else... gone.
    t ARIA... gone.
    
    
    t The distress beacon is blinking. Someone will find me.
    t They have to find me.
    
    
    goto ending_escape
